2025-11-29 21:35:56 - metadata_extractor.services.hardware_crawler - INFO - LLM extract prompt len=303103 preview='You are a data extraction agent. Given HTML content from a trusted hardware catalog at https://www.techpowerup.com/gpu-specs/ (and any of its subdomains),\nreturn a JSON array of hardware objects with this exact shape:\n- hardware_id: a stable, non-empty string identifier (e.g., slugified vendor + model + kind)\n- kind: one of ["cpu_node", "gpu", "tpu", "accelerator", "jetson", "soc"]\n- vendor: string\n- model_name: string\n- spec: object matching the kind-specific requirements below\n- url: product URL if present\n- price: REQUIRED if shown on the page (release price/MSRP or listed price, include currency). If no price is explicitly present in the HTML, set price to null (never invent or estimate).\n- source: set to the source URL\n\nSpec requirements:\n- cpu_node:\n  - Required numbers: num_sockets, cores_per_socket, threads_per_core (ints >0)\n  - Required numbers: base_clock_ghz, vector_width_bits, fma_units_per_core (>0)\n  - Required memory: ram_capacity_gb (>0) AND (ram_bandwidth_gbps OR (mem...'
